<title>GERMANY: Daimler sees 97 unit car sales at 700,000.</title>
<headline>Daimler sees 97 unit car sales at 700,000.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG Chairman Juergen Schrempp said on Wednesday he expected 1997 car sales to climb to over 700,000 from 645,000 in 1996.</p>
<p>He also said European truck orders were up 45 percent in the first four months of 1997.</p>
<p>Speaking at Daimler's annual meeting, Schrempp repeated that he expected car divission profit to remain at about the same level as last year.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite the high cost associated with new products, we assume that the profit will remain at the same high level as in 1996,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
